title: ch2_box_net60
---
A furniture warehouse offers steady routes, five days a week. Their terms are net 60. #line:ch2_box_net60_01
Fuel, tolls and your driver's pay are due every week. #line:ch2_box_net60_02
-> Ask for net 30 and a deposit. #line:ch2_box_net60_03
    <<choose "negotiate">>
    They agree to net 30 if you start Monday. You start Monday. #line:ch2_box_net60_04
-> Accept net 60 as it is. #line:ch2_box_net60_05
    <<choose "accept">>
    The work pours in. The money arrives two months later. #line:ch2_box_net60_06
===

title: ch2_box_fuel
---
Diesel jumps forty cents a gallon overnight. Your contracts don't say who pays for that. #line:ch2_box_fuel_01
-> Add a fuel surcharge to new invoices. #line:ch2_box_fuel_02
    <<choose "surcharge">>
    Most clients accept it. The industry does it, and now so do you. #line:ch2_box_fuel_03
-> Absorb it and hope prices fall. #line:ch2_box_fuel_04
    <<choose "eat">>
    They don't, this month. #line:ch2_box_fuel_05
===

title: ch2_box_overweight
